.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt CONV 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm conv
.Nd convert one value from standard input to standard output
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl hV
.Ar from
.Ar to
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads one value from standard input and writes it to standard output.
It reads no files and takes no configuration.
.Ar from
and
.Ar to
name the input and output encodings.
Names are case-insensitive.
.Pp
A data error is one line on standard error, prefixed with
.Dq conv: ,
and standard output is left empty.
A usage error is reported by the argument parser.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-V, --version"
.It Fl h , Fl \-help
Display this help and exit.
.It Fl V , Fl \-version
Output version information and exit.
.El
.Sh FORMATS
.Bl -tag -width "www-form"
.It Cm json
One value.
Output is compact.
.It Cm yaml
One document.
.Cm yml
is an alias.
.It Cm toml
One document.
The root must be a table, and null is an error.
.It Cm ron
One value.
.It Cm url
A query string.
Values are strings.
.Cm www\-form
is an alias.
.It Cm cbor
Raw bytes, as in RFC 8949.
.It Cm msgpack
Raw bytes.
.El
.Pp
.Cm json ,
.Cm yaml ,
.Cm toml ,
.Cm ron ,
and
.Cm url
are text and end with a newline.
.Cm cbor
and
.Cm msgpack
are raw bytes, including when standard output is a terminal.
.Pp
Input is one value.
A second value or other trailing data is an error, and nothing is written.
Comments, anchors, and tags are not preserved.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 2n
.It 0
The conversion succeeded.
.It 1
The value could not be converted.
.It 2
There was a usage error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Convert JSON on standard input to TOML:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
echo \(aq{"abc": 123}\(aq | conv json toml
.Ed
.Pp
Convert YAML on standard input to JSON:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
conv yaml json
.Ed
